findings.body:
The condition at `src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py:397` changed from `full_name not in deployment_names` to `dep.name not in deployment_names`. The original line was correct. For a short filter such as `--deployment production`, `dep.name` (`"production"`) is in the list, so the whole matching block is skipped. The `short_name_matches` bookkeeping never runs, and the ambiguity warning for a short name matching several flows is never produced. The existing test `test_fetch_sdk_data_ambiguous_short_name_warning` (tests/_sdk/test_fetcher.py:581-597) asserts exactly that warning, so it should fail.

For full-name filters the result is accidentally the same, but only because the inner loop still performs the exact match. The change has no stated purpose in the PR description, and it is not covered by any new test.

