The "Combine multiple filters" example in `generate-custom-sdk.mdx` passes `--flow etl-flow --flow data-sync --deployment analytics/daily`. In `fetch_sdk_data`, the flow filter and the deployment filter are both sent to one `read_deployments(flow_filter=..., deployment_filter=...)` call, so they are ANDed on the server. A deployment in the `analytics` flow cannot match a flow filter for `etl-flow` or `data-sync`. The command therefore raises `NoDeploymentsError`, which the CLI reports as "No deployments found".

The guide should either drop the `--flow` options from this example or show a combination that is actually valid. It should also say how the filters combine, since users will reasonably expect OR across flags.

::code{file="docs/v3/advanced/generate-custom-sdk.mdx" lines="40-46"}

::callout{type="warning"}
If the intended behavior is OR across `--flow` and `--deployment`, the fix belongs in the fetcher, not the docs. The current code is AND.

`_fetch_work_pool` used to check `isinstance(variables, dict)` before assigning `job_vars_schema`. That check is now gone at `src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py:181-182`. The variable is still annotated `dict[str, Any]`, but a `"variables"` key with a `null` or list value now flows straight through. The renderer reads `work_pool.job_variables_schema` (`src/prefect/_sdk/renderer.py:271`) and passes it on to the schema converter, which expects a mapping. A malformed or unusual work pool template could then crash generation with an unclear error. The PR does not explain why the guard was removed.

::diff{file="src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py" lines="180-183"}

If the guard was removed to satisfy a type checker, restore it or narrow the type explicitly. Degrading to `{}` with a warning matches how the rest of this function handles bad work pools.

The new `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` sits between `import prefect` and the `from prefect._sdk.models import (...)` block, at `src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py:19-21`. Every import after it becomes a non-top-level import. Running `ruff check src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py` in the repo's venv reports four errors, including E402 at line 36. CI lint will fail on this.

Move the logger definition below the full import block, next to the other module-level definitions.

::diff{file="src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py" lines="19-22"}

In `_fetch_work_pools_parallel`, `zip(pool_names_list, results, strict=True)` became a plain `zip(...)` (`src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py:220`). Both lists come from the same comprehension and `gather` preserves length, so the behavior is unchanged today. `strict=True` is still a cheap guard against a future edit that desynchronizes them, and the repo's ruff config does not require removing it. The change looks unrelated to the docs PR.

::diff{file="src/prefect/_sdk/fetcher.py" lines="219-221"}

Restore `strict=True` unless there is a specific reason to drop it.
